---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { appConfig, isConfiguredEmail } from '../config/app';
const ready = isConfiguredEmail(appConfig.privacyEmail);
---
<BaseLayout title="Account deletion | HealthWallet" description="Instructions for deleting a HealthWallet account and associated app data.">
  <div class="inner-hero"><div class="container"><span class="section-kicker">Manage your data</span><h1>Delete your account</h1><p>How to delete your HealthWallet account in the app, and how to ask for help if you cannot sign in.</p></div></div>
  <div class="container content-wrap">
    {!ready && <aside class="notice"><strong>Privacy email still required</strong>Set a monitored privacy inbox in <code>src/config/app.ts</code> so people who cannot sign in have a way to ask for deletion. This notice disappears once it is set.</aside>}
    <section class="legal-section"><h2>Delete in the app</h2><ol class="steps"><li>Sign in to HealthWallet.</li><li>Open <strong>Settings</strong> and scroll to the <strong>Account</strong> section.</li><li>Tap <strong>Delete account</strong>.</li><li>Read the confirmation dialog, type <strong>DELETE</strong>, and confirm. The app deletes your account and signs you out.</li></ol><p class="muted">If the app shows a failure message, the deletion did not complete. Contact support for help.</p></section>
    <section class="legal-section"><h2>What is deleted</h2><p>HealthWallet first removes the files you uploaded — your profile photo, medical documents and progress photos — and then deletes your account. With it go your profile and health information, appointments, chats and the messages you sent, notifications, plans assigned to you, reports and blocks that involve you, and the app's record of your payments.</p><p>A doctor's public map listing can remain as directory information, no longer connected to the account. Backups kept by our database provider are overwritten within 7 days. FIB keeps its own payment records under its own obligations. The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> has the details.</p></section>
    <section class="legal-section"><h2>Cannot access your account?</h2><p>Request deletion at {ready ? <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.privacyEmail}`}>{appConfig.privacyEmail}</a> : <strong>{appConfig.privacyEmail}</strong>}. Include the phone number linked to the account and say that you want to delete your HealthWallet account. Do not send a verification code or medical records by email. We will confirm the request comes from the account holder before deleting anything.</p></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
